WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.988
Pick a plan, press Start ride, and Wattzup drives the bike for you.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.696
Set up your ride. HIIT intervals are hard and easy efforts on repeat, and the

00:00:12.696 --> 00:00:15.314
resistance switches at every interval.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.788
Press Tabata: eight rounds of twenty seconds on, and ten off.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.609
The preview adds up the ride before you start.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.460
Start ride sends the plan. Starting, then the dashboard.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.363
Here you are in round five of eight: work at level eighteen, with half a minute to

00:00:40.363 --> 00:00:40.823
go.

00:00:41.023 --> 00:00:44.083
Next: recover for twenty seconds at level six.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.481
When a segment starts, the plan sends its level to the bike.

00:00:51.681 --> 00:00:55.807
Sent to bike lists every command, and the bike acknowledges each one.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.066
Every change is called out. Work, eighteen, go!

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.675
Power versus plan draws your effort against every target.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.483
On a phone, the dashboard is one column.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.792
On a desktop, the resistance sits beside it.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.605
What no screen shows: if the bike drifts off the level, the plan sends it again

00:01:32.605 --> 00:01:34.013
every five seconds.

00:01:34.213 --> 00:01:36.887
And if a send fails, the ride keeps going.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.022
That is journey one. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live training

00:01:43.022 --> 00:01:43.800
display.
